    <string name="settings_m3_how_step1_title">Your vaults, on Android</string>
    <string name="settings_m3_how_step1_body">Clone from GitHub, any Git host or over SSH. Each vault keeps its own connection and branch.</string>
    <string name="settings_m3_how_step2_title">Edit where you like</string>
    <string name="settings_m3_how_step2_body">Write here, or keep the vault in a device folder and use Obsidian. Check folder access in Settings before you clone.</string>
    <string name="settings_m3_how_step3_title">Review, then publish</string>
    <string name="settings_m3_how_step3_body">See the diff, pick what to stage and commit on the phone. Push when you’re ready. Branches, history, tags, conflicts and LFS live in the vault.</string>
    <string name="settings_m3_how_step4_title">Let it catch up</string>
    <string name="settings_m3_how_step4_body">Background Sync pulls on a schedule. Push Sync pulls when GitHub changes. Neither commits for you unless you say so.</string>

